{
  "slug": "user-story-and-acceptance-criteria",
  "concept": "User Story and Acceptance Criteria",
  "generated": "2026-09-08",
  "summary": "This skill takes a feature idea and produces backlog items the team can groom, estimate, and ship. Covers Mike Cohn's user-story template, the INVEST quality bar (Bill Wake, 2003), Given/When/Then acc",
  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "This skill takes a feature idea and produces backlog items the team can groom, estimate, and ship. Covers Mike Cohn's user-story template, the INVEST quality bar (Bill Wake, 2003), Given/When/Then acceptance criteria in Gherkin form, splitting strategies (vertical-slice principle and SPIDR), and the separation between acceptance criteria (per-story, varies) and definition of done (team-wide, stable).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#overview",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "1. The Mike Cohn user-story template",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "As a <role> - the user, not the system. \"As a user\" is the most common failure mode. Name a specific actor type: \"As a job seeker\", \"As an on-call TAM\", \"As a paid subscriber on the Pro tier.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#1-the-mike-cohn-user-story-template",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "I want <capability> - the what, written goal-first, agnostic to how.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#1-the-mike-cohn-user-story-template",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "so that <benefit> - the why. The benefit clause is the most-skipped and most-valuable.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#1-the-mike-cohn-user-story-template",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2. INVEST — the quality bar",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "I - Independent. The story can be built, demoed, and shipped without waiting on another story.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#2-invest-the-quality-bar",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "N - Negotiable. The story is a placeholder for a conversation, not a contract.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#2-invest-the-quality-bar",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "V - Valuable. The story delivers value to a real user or stakeholder.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#2-invest-the-quality-bar",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "E - Estimable. The team has enough context to size it.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#2-invest-the-quality-bar",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "S - Small. Fits comfortably inside an iteration. Heuristic: ≤ 50% of one developer's iteration capacity.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#2-invest-the-quality-bar",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "T - Testable. A definite test exists for \"done.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#2-invest-the-quality-bar",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3. Given / When / Then — Gherkin acceptance criteria",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "And and But chain steps in the same phase.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#3-given-when-then-gherkin-acceptance-criteria",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "3–5 steps per scenario.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#3-given-when-then-gherkin-acceptance-criteria",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "1–3 acceptance criteria per story.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#3-given-when-then-gherkin-acceptance-criteria",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Each criterion tests a distinct aspect.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#3-given-when-then-gherkin-acceptance-criteria",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Concrete values, not generics: \"Given a charge of $20.00\" not \"Given a valid charge.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#3-given-when-then-gherkin-acceptance-criteria",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "4. The vertical slice rule",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "A user story must be a thin vertical slice through the architecture - a sliver that touches every layer and delivers end-to-end value.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#4-the-vertical-slice-rule",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Horizontal (wrong):",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#4-the-vertical-slice-rule",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Story 1: Build the UI for case filtering.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#4-the-vertical-slice-rule",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Story 2: Build the API endpoint for case filtering.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#4-the-vertical-slice-rule",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Story 3: Add the database index for case filtering.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#4-the-vertical-slice-rule",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Vertical (right):",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#4-the-vertical-slice-rule",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Story 1: Filter cases by severity (S1 only, no UI persistence).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#4-the-vertical-slice-rule",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Story 2: Filter cases by status, with severity already shipped.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#4-the-vertical-slice-rule",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "5. SPIDR — five ways to split a story",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "S - Spike. Time-box a research task to remove uncertainty blocking estimation.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#5-spidr-five-ways-to-split-a-story",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "P - Path. Split by user path. \"Pay with credit card\" / \"Pay with Apple Pay.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#5-spidr-five-ways-to-split-a-story",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "I - Interface. Split by client or platform. \"Filter cases on desktop\" / \"Filter cases in mobile app.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#5-spidr-five-ways-to-split-a-story",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "D - Data. Split by data scope. \"Filter cases for active accounts only\" first; \"including archived accounts\" later.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#5-spidr-five-ways-to-split-a-story",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "R - Rules. Relax business rules in the first slice. \"Refunds, with no approval workflow\" first; \"Refunds with manager-approval workflow\" later.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#5-spidr-five-ways-to-split-a-story",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "6. Acceptance criteria vs Definition of Done",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Acceptance Criteria (AC):",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#6-acceptance-criteria-vs-definition-of-done",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Specific to this story.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#6-acceptance-criteria-vs-definition-of-done",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Authored by the product owner with the team.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#6-acceptance-criteria-vs-definition-of-done",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Vary between stories.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#6-acceptance-criteria-vs-definition-of-done",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Answer: \"What must this story do for the user to accept it?\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#6-acceptance-criteria-vs-definition-of-done",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Definition of Done (DoD):",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#6-acceptance-criteria-vs-definition-of-done",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "A team-wide standard that applies to every story.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#6-acceptance-criteria-vs-definition-of-done",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Stable across sprints.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#6-acceptance-criteria-vs-definition-of-done",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Answers: \"What must any item meet to be called done?\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#6-acceptance-criteria-vs-definition-of-done",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "A story is done when both its acceptance criteria are met and the team's definition of done is satisfied.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#6-acceptance-criteria-vs-definition-of-done",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Anti-Patterns",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "\"As a user, I want...\" - every story starts the same way, tells you nothing.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Solution-shaped capability clauses - \"I want a dropdown in the top-right corner.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "No so that clause - strips out the prioritization signal.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Horizontal-layer stories (\"Build the backend for X\") - each is independently unshippable.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Acceptance criteria that restate the story.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "20-criterion acceptance lists - the story is too big. Split.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Conflating Acceptance Criteria with Definition of Done.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Forcing bugs / tech-debt / spikes into user-story syntax.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Decision Heuristics",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "\"As a user\" or a specific role? Always specific.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#decision-heuristics",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Story or epic? If the story has > 1 sprint of work or > 5 acceptance criteria, it's an epic. Split via SPIDR.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#decision-heuristics",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Gherkin or checklist for AC? Gherkin when multi-step interactions or branching. Checklist when criteria are independent observable facts.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#decision-heuristics",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Put it in AC or in DoD? Specific to this story → AC. Applies to every story → DoD.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/user-story-and-acceptance-criteria/#decision-heuristics",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
